WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:06.588
npm security matters because modern
Node.js applications are built from many layers

2
00:00:06.668 --> 00:00:11.911
of first-party code, open source packages,
build tools, test utilities,

3
00:00:11.991 --> 00:00:15.627
transitive dependencies, and registry
metadata.

4
00:00:15.707 --> 00:00:21.541
A small application can depend on hundreds
or thousands of packages after the full

5
00:00:21.621 --> 00:00:23.735
dependency tree is resolved.

6
00:00:23.815 --> 00:00:28.381
That dependency tree becomes part of the
software supply chain,

7
00:00:28.461 --> 00:00:33.112
even when most of the code was not written
by the application team.

8
00:00:33.192 --> 00:00:36.743
The risk is not limited to known
vulnerabilities.

9
00:00:36.823 --> 00:00:39.952
Package installation can execute scripts,

10
00:00:40.032 --> 00:00:44.936
dependency updates can change behavior,
maintainership can shift,

11
00:00:45.016 --> 00:00:47.553
account credentials can be stolen,

12
00:00:47.633 --> 00:00:52.791
and internal package names can collide
with public registry packages if

13
00:00:52.871 --> 00:00:54.562
configuration is weak.

14
00:00:54.642 --> 00:00:56.925
npm gives teams enormous speed,

15
00:00:57.005 --> 00:01:02.163
but speed only stays useful when teams
understand how packages enter the

16
00:01:02.243 --> 00:01:05.203
environment, how versions are selected,

17
00:01:05.283 --> 00:01:09.511
and how changes are reviewed before they
reach production.

18
00:01:09.591 --> 00:01:15.087
A practical npm security program does not
try to eliminate third-party code.

19
00:01:15.167 --> 00:01:19.733
It treats package use as an engineering
decision with evidence,

20
00:01:19.813 --> 00:01:22.857
review, reproducibility, and ownership.

21
00:01:22.937 --> 00:01:27.673
Developers should know what they are
installing, why it is needed,

22
00:01:27.753 --> 00:01:33.756
how it is locked, how findings are
triaged, and how CI/CD prevents accidental drift.

23
00:01:33.836 --> 00:01:39.586
The goal is a workflow where dependency
risk is visible and manageable instead of

24
00:01:39.666 --> 00:01:41.780
hidden inside node_modules.
